{
 "name": "noseat-dose",
 "note": "DOSE-RESPONSE test for kd-riXXp2Yvty. v1 and v2 both read 0/48 with a ~33% collapse in town lifetime off a ~2-3% event, which is disproportionate enough that the arm must be falsified before it is reported. dose0 runs EVERY line of the hatch (the second pickSeat call, the counter, the stat) and walks NOBODY out: it MUST come back byte-identical to ctl, or the plumbing perturbs the stream it measures and no reading here means anything. dose50 fires on every other eligible guest: a real economic effect shows dose-response, a plumbing artifact does not. ctl re-taken in-run; must reproduce ~7/48.",
